{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038198-trauma-therapy-and-the-changing-paradigm","id":1038198,"title":"Trauma, Therapy and The Changing paradigm","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-25T19:34:29-08:00","id":1038198,"title":"Trauma, Therapy and The Changing paradigm","content":"So, soon im going to run the Horizon War and im already considering the aftermath on the PC's.<br /> <br /> i was wondering if any book mentions how do mages deal with mental traumas, PTSD and such. i been thinking if its possible for a mage to recieve such a strong mental trauma that he whitdraws and even 'forgets'/fears to do any magical effects (in a way, shutting his own avatar down or put it in a 'coma').<br /> <br /> One of the pc's is going to have his mindshattered and will be find in earth rambling insanely and being taken into a sleeper mental facility to cope with his traumas.<br /> while other Pc is going to turn out to heavy drugs to try to escape the demons and horrors of the horizon war.<br /> <br /> also, its it possible that a mage's paradigm shifts due to heavy trauma or to cope with personal pain?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T19:53:20-08:00","id":1038210,"title":"","content":"Take a look at the rules of Quiet. If you wanted, you could have your mages get PTSD infused flashbacks which recreate themselves right infront of the mage themselves. They hear something that sounds like an explosion, suddenly it is an explosion. The see a shape which reminds them of a HIT mark, A HIT mark appears and chases your group for as long as the PTSD'd mage imagines them being around.<br /> But that's just for Dynamic style Quiets, you could also have Static style quiets where they are fixated on one particular version of reality, and anything that doesn't fit it simply does not exist.<br /> <br /> Another thing you could do is Mindscapes, where the mage is trapped within their own mental torture. Their body is effectively catatonic, and they may need a few psychonauts to help them out of it.<br /> <br /> These kinds of events can lead to things like Seekings, and indeed may result in a Paradigm shift if things get really twisted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T20:03:56-08:00","id":1038220,"title":"","content":"If a Mage goes through a stressful, traumatic event, and they don't believe their existing Paradigm can or did help them get through it, they may very well shift to a Paradigm that could. It doesn't matter if the new Paradigm actually would be better for them, they just have to think it would at the time. People alter their worldviews all the time in response to changing circumstance. One of the examples cited in M20 was the fallout from the horrors of WWI, which caused mass abandonment of the previous era's optimism. It's difficult to believe in an inevitable societal progress towards Utopia - prevalent in the Victorian period - when you were made to cower in a trench, fearful of artillery shells and mustard gas, as a result of petty and short-sighted political decisions made by distant kings and diplomats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T20:17:51-08:00","id":1038236,"title":"","content":"so in theory is possible for a goody two shoes from the order of hermes turn into a John Fucking Constantine type due to the trauma","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T21:55:52-08:00","id":1038267,"title":"","content":"<i>If the roleplaying shakes out that way</i>, yes. It's possible for a goody two-shoes to become a cynical jerk. Especially as a result of war. Whether the <i>player</i> will take the character that route is another point entirely. Just as some people alter their worldview as a result of trauma, other people dig deeper into the one they have. It depends on the person and their individual circumstances.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T19:32:09-08:00","id":1042180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038198-trauma-therapy-and-the-changing-paradigm#post1038198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the pc's is going to have his mindshattered and will be find in earth rambling insanely and being taken into a sleeper mental facility to cope with his traumas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, unless it's Sleepers doing it, that's not wont to happen. Mages take care of their own, especially when you take into consideration the unfortunate bastard still has an Arete rating and if that individual decides to put it to use, no Sleeper on the planet is like to deal with it and traditional means of subduing out-of-control patients can and <i>will</i> make matters worse. I don't see any scenario where shooting an Ecstatic full of sedatives, or administering electroshock therapy to a Hermetic, for example, turns out well for the Sleeper doing it.<br /> <br /> Not to mention, the Technocracy's still out there, and watching mental institutions for Mages --, either newly-awakened, Orphans with no idea who or what they really are, or in the throes of Quiet -- is something they do. A mage getting checked into a Sleeper mental facility, for all the record-keeping health care professionals do, is a quick way to earn a ticket to Room 101.<br /> <br /> But, all of that pales in comparison to <a href=\"http://imgur.com/X9Mh64I\" target=\"_blank\">the shade realm-sized elephant in the room</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T20:09:48-08:00","id":1042195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038198-trauma-therapy-and-the-changing-paradigm?p=1042180#post1042180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, unless it's Sleepers doing it, that's not wont to happen. Mages take care of their own, especially when you take into consideration the unfortunate bastard still has an Arete rating and if that individual decides to put it to use, no Sleeper on the planet is like to deal with it and traditional means of subduing out-of-control patients can and <i>will</i> make matters worse. I don't see any scenario where shooting an Ecstatic full of sedatives, or administering electroshock therapy to a Hermetic, for example, turns out well for the Sleeper doing it.<br /> <br /> Not to mention, the Technocracy's still out there, and watching mental institutions for Mages --, either newly-awakened, Orphans with no idea who or what they really are, or in the throes of Quiet -- is something they do. A mage getting checked into a Sleeper mental facility, for all the record-keeping health care professionals do, is a quick way to earn a ticket to Room 101.<br /> <br /> But, all of that pales in comparison to <a href=\"http://imgur.com/X9Mh64I\" target=\"_blank\">the shade realm-sized elephant in the room</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even in Mage society, certain people slip through the cracks.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, the facility is being run by Marauders who genuinely believe that Madness leads to Greatness, so they must make more Madness in order to achieve more Greatness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T20:25:11-08:00","id":1042207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038198-trauma-therapy-and-the-changing-paradigm?p=1042195#post1042195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even in Mage society, certain people slip through the cracks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Slipping through the cracks is one thing. What happens next is entirely different.<br /> <br /> A known mage with mental problems going missing, who may very well be in Quiet and/or gone Marauder, is invariably a multiple-alarm fire that needs to be put out RFN. Your best-case scenario is the mage stays low, snaps out of it eventually, and comes back to the fold, but that's really only going to happen if the mage retains control of their mental faculties enough to lay low in the first place. Even in the best conditions, that's about as far from a foregone conclusion as you can get, and no cabal in the right mind would ever bet on it.<br /> <br /> The safe bet is <i>always </i>to work from the default assumption the missing mage is a walking time bomb, and a danger to themselves, nearby Sleepers, their cabal, and possibly their Tradition, if not from their own activities then <i>definitely</i> the Technocracy who'll be after them with a vengeance once that mage peeks their head up in the least.<br /> <br /> There's a reason there's a whole lot of ink spilled about mages with mental problems, even if they're not in Quiet or Marauders, the dangers they pose to themselves and others, and the lengths other mages go to protect them and those around them, on both sides of the fence, starting from the VE Convention book on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 02-01-2017, 11:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T20:29:03-08:00","id":1042209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038198-trauma-therapy-and-the-changing-paradigm?p=1042207#post1042207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Slipping through the cracks is one thing. What happens next is entirely different.<br /> <br /> A known mage with mental problems going missing, who may very well be in Quiet and/or gone Marauder, is invariably a multiple-alarm fire that needs to be put out RFN. Your best-case scenario is the mage stays low, snaps out of it eventually, and comes back to the fold, but that's really only going to happen if the mage retains control of their mental faculties enough to lay low in the first place. Even in the best conditions, that's about as far from a foregone conclusion as you can get, and no cabal in the right mind would ever bet on it.<br /> <br /> The safe bet is <i>always </i>to work from the default assumption the missing mage is a walking time bomb, and a danger to themselves, nearby Sleepers, their cabal, and possibly their Tradition, if not from their own activities then <i>definitely</i> the Technocracy who'll be after them with a vengeance once that mage peeks their head up in the least.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your assuming the mages in question are A) Aware of everything that's going on. B) Don't have bigger time bombs to sort out RFN. C) Thought someone else had already taken care of it. D) Actually think the mage turning marauder can be an advantage to them for...reasons.<br /> <br /> Not all Mages do sensible things. Most of them do outright stupid things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T20:46:30-08:00","id":1042212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038198-trauma-therapy-and-the-changing-paradigm?p=1042209#post1042209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your assuming the mages in question are A) Aware of everything that's going on. B) Don't have bigger time bombs to sort out RFN. C) Thought someone else had already taken care of it. D) Actually think the mage turning marauder can be an advantage to them for...reasons.<br /> <br /> Not all Mages do sensible things. Most of them do outright stupid things.</div> </div> </div> </div>A) They don't have to be. &quot;Hey, where's Bob?&quot; is a pretty basic question with, in most circumstances, a fairly simple answer usually found in some iteration of readily-available Life, Mind, Spirit, and/or Prime, and in any case Correspondence, Effects made all the easier due to sympathetic links between Cabal-mates. &quot;I can't find Bob&quot; is the nightmare answer to that otherwise fairly basic question with a simple answer. Because...<br /> <br /> B) Missing mages <i>are</i> most Tradition mages' worst-case scenario, against which everything up to and maybe even including the imminent collapse of Reality itself goes on the backburner. Missing mages are a treasure troves of intel just waiting for the Technocracy to find; if mages are one thing it's self-interested, and they're not about to let somebody with insight into their own schemes fall into Technocratic hands.<br /> <br /> C) and D), well, stupid mages are stupid. Letting a cabal-mate fall into Technocratic hands due to not having taken a token effort to find them falls perfectly within the &quot;stupid&quot; category. It's pretty much Exhibit A in the case of a given mage being stupid, there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T20:57:02-08:00","id":1042217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038198-trauma-therapy-and-the-changing-paradigm?p=1042212#post1042212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A) They don't have to be. &amp;quot;Hey, where's Bob?&amp;quot; is a pretty basic question with, in most circumstances, a fairly simple answer usually found in some iteration of readily-available Life, Mind, Spirit, and/or Prime, and in any case Correspondence, Effects made all the easier due to sympathetic links between Cabal-mates. &amp;quot;I can't find Bob&amp;quot; is the nightmare answer to that otherwise fairly basic question with a simple answer. Because...<br /> <br /> B) Missing mages <i>are</i> most Tradition mages' worst-case scenario, against which everything up to and maybe even including the imminent collapse of Reality itself goes on the backburner. Missing mages are a treasure troves of intel just waiting for the Technocracy to find; if mages are one thing it's self-interested, and they're not about to let somebody with insight into their own schemes fall into Technocratic hands.<br /> <br /> C) and D), well, stupid mages are stupid. Letting a cabal-mate fall into Technocratic hands due to not having taken a token effort to find them falls perfectly within the &amp;quot;stupid&amp;quot; category. It's pretty much Exhibit A in the case of a given mage being stupid, there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I usually find the more intelligent the mage, the more stupid they can be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T21:01:06-08:00","id":1042218,"title":"","content":"Strangely enough, the one place where a mentally unstable Mage could go and be undetectable would be the Far Dreaming (Mystical Mage can see into the Near Dreaming without forgetting everything because of their low Banality). The Mists make the insane Mage forget their life in the Autumn World, which may be what the Mage seeks, and the chimera of his dreams surround him and protect him from harm. If he accepts insanity, the Dreaming will allow him to remain in the Far Dreaming and will even allow him to do True Magick as long as he follows Its rules. The problem for anyone trying to find him is they are unlikely to be so lucky because they will be trying to retain their sanity so they can save him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T21:13:01-08:00","id":1042219,"title":"","content":"I think it comes down to two questions: 1) Does the cabal-mate make a habit of disappearing for extended periods of time, and 2) Does the cabal care about the particular Mage in question?<br /> <br /> As a corallary to the latter, did the cabal have cause to believe the cabalmate is unwell? If the Mage was displaying signs of mental instability as a result of the war they just fought, that's all the cause they need to be suspicious if they suddenly disappear. Don't forget, also, that War is a known traumatic phenomenon, and one of the basic questions that might come up when they come back from it would be &quot;Are you feeling okay?&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm not saying it's a sure thing, or that the cabal can't be distracted or willing to let a snap of &quot;I'm fine!&quot; go without pressing. But the act of showing interest in a cabalmates well-being makes a concerted search more likely if that cabalmate later goes missing. It depends on the cabal (and the players running them), and what they have going on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T21:15:19-08:00","id":1042220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038198-trauma-therapy-and-the-changing-paradigm?p=1042218#post1042218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Strangely enough, the one place where a mentally unstable Mage could go and be undetectable would be the Far Dreaming (Mystical Mage can see into the Near Dreaming without forgetting everything because of their low Banality). The Mists make the insane Mage forget their life in the Autumn World, which may be what the Mage seeks, and the chimera of his dreams surround him and protect him from harm. If he accepts insanity, the Dreaming will allow him to remain in the Far Dreaming and will even allow him to do True Magick as long as he follows Its rules. The problem for anyone trying to find him is they are unlikely to be so lucky because they will be trying to retain their sanity so they can save him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, this ignores <a href=\"http://imgur.com/X9Mh64I\" target=\"_blank\">a realm-sized elephant in the room</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}